"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d9f525c4d5985d6aa8793a8be364b558d2b13f59fa68f5eb3b50e0d77a796da" "basis" 1255 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The height $H$ of a tree increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the tree's height at that moment.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height $H?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d9f525c4d5985d6aa8793a8be364b558d2b13f59fa68f5eb3b50e0d77a796da" "basis" 1255 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of a tree **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **tree's height** $H$ at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *tree's height.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{H}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d9f525c4d5985d6aa8793a8be364b558d2b13f59fa68f5eb3b50e0d77a796da" "basis" 1255 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043" "basis" 1255 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d9f525c4d5985d6aa8793a8be364b558d2b13f59fa68f5eb3b50e0d77a796da" "basis" 1255 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d9f525c4d5985d6aa8793a8be364b558d2b13f59fa68f