**inversely proportional** to the **tree's height** $H$ at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *tree's height.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{H}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041088/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a3fb445dedee98736c8722f34b39bd97162cee6050a2cd720a0f4c5f2b1e0eb"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b2878443cc0008e933413ef7a22fc8902a26adb7c74953e2c18905a7f30118ab"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041088/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a3fb445dedee98736c8722f34b39bd97162cee6050a2cd720a0f4c5f2b1e0eb"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\tex